---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="Two overlapping open books and three speech-bubble shapes, flat gold and black on warm cream, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Every week you build and run a small instrument against a piece of
    reasoning — yours, a classmate's, or a fabricated one — and report what it
    detected, what it missed, and what it couldn't tell you at all. The
    artefact you leave with is not a portfolio of answers; it's a record of
    which of your own claims to understand something actually held up under
    a test you designed yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has caught themselves saying "I get it" a beat too quickly —
    after a lecture, a tutorial, a fluent answer from an AI. No prior subject
    knowledge is assumed, because the course is domain-neutral: you supply
    the material you already half-know, and the course supplies the pressure.
    It will suit you badly if you want a settled answer by the final week;
    that's not on offer here.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
